      'The myth about his death also matters. Communities sometimes keep myths because they express a truth about fear and experience. But an encyclopedia has to do something more careful: honor the real history without repeating false details. The true story of Drew\'s life already contains enough evidence of racism, brilliance, service, and consequence. It does not need an invented final scene.'
